{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## First external batch filtering checkpoint\n\nEvidence revision: origin/main 6a5c88027c59d3e24d3e4269838fb3c591a64240. Every proposal-relevant file is unchanged from the inspected 4d6c1cc baseline. Targeted tracker searches found no active implementation owner for these defects beyond this audit.\n\n- F08A RETAIN. Limit this unit to factual README workflow corrections. Name all seven relations including caused_by. Document optional relation-scoped unlink. Omit an explicit claim assignee in the generic path and explain that an override must be Jira-resolvable. Correct help-token placement to match the any-position-before-double-dash dispatcher rule. Correct completion-gate coverage for task, bug, story, and epic closes. Preserve the tested quickstart and do not restructure the README.\n- F08B RETAIN. Limit this unit to README installation facts. The mcp extra is mcp 1.28.1 through the next major plus PyJWT crypto. Base installs have three dependencies, including referencing. The agents extra includes Anthropic while Bedrock has its own extra and OpenAI or Google provider groups require separate installation. Git 2.38 is the development and test floor, not an unconditional runtime floor.\n- F09 REVISE. Split the work into external signing and help guidance, internal event and API reference, and gate trust-model guidance. New sign operations and the plan-review and completion-verifier certificate kinds use DSSE envelopes with SSHSIG and Ed25519. HMAC remains only for legacy read compatibility and separate implemented consumers. Edit canonical parser help before regenerating packaged help and the CLI reference. Preserve intentional compatibility and historical statements.\n- F10 REVISE. Keep the import user contract but correct canonical ownership. src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py owns packaged import help. Update it before regenerating help and the CLI reference. docs/import-export.md must describe 256-event batching for create, parent, file-impact or verify-command, and comment passes. Links and statuses remain per-event. Push occurs only after successful completion. Serial reruns skip existing source_id values but do not complete a ticket left after a create-only crash. Concurrent imports can duplicate when both scans precede either write. Document partial results and supported recovery without changing importer behavior.\n- F12 REVISE. The RP-05 dependency tickets are closed, but the ADR 0100 help contract remains unmet. scripts/gen_cli_help.py excludes the 21 visible pure-intercept routes from packaged overview help. rebar help review-plan fails while rebar review-plan --help succeeds. Scope this as a help-only conformance fix through the existing route registry, parser factories, generators, and runtime artifact reader. Do not add a router or parser path.\n- F13 RETAIN. scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py uses the first physical description line, which emits incomplete summaries such as transition_ticket ending in Returns the. Normalize the first description paragraph, stop before the next paragraph, regenerate docs/mcp-reference.md, and add focused generator tests. Do not add a prose validator. The transition registrar already states current close semantics and does not need a behavior change.\n- F19 REVISE. Split this into three units. First remove the false generated claim of an MCP config-transparency surface because no such tool exists. Second establish explicit public configuration metadata before the generated reference claims exhaustive external coverage. Third make bounded current-state corrections in docs/config.md, including the cross-ticket overlap citation to ADR 0086 and transport retry citation to ADR 0087. These units do not decide or depend on deferred F05.\n\nSequencing: complete F12 before final README help wording. Serialize F08A, F08B, and the README portion of F09 because they share README.md. For each generated family, edit the canonical source before packaged help and generated references. No project file changed during this filter."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787415554701976001,"uuid":"3645c372-99f9-4d73-ae05-ab4cfc9ed642"}